# The script the fixture harness runs stepped (`fixture-test`;
# docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate runs a fixture") against
# the config in `config/`, which chooses a left edge of 25 percent round
# master-and-stack, sends the buffers of the minor mode `notes` to that
# edge, and binds `C-c n` to a command that makes such a buffer and
# displays it. It shows the docked window in its strip, focused by
# direction, moved into the tiles and back with `C-w H`, promoted to main
# with `C-w m` and closed with `C-w C-c`, as any window is, and the last
# tile refused at an edge with the reason in the echo area. What it prints
# must be exactly `expected`. It touches no file.

reload
settle

# A frame of 640 by 480: the tiled area is 640 by 464, above the bottom row.
resize 640 480

# `C-c n` docks `notes` at the left edge: its strip is 160 pixels wide,
# main has the rest, and the new window is focused.
key c KeyC control
key n KeyN -
scene

# `C-w l` focuses main, beside the strip, and `C-w h` the docked window
# again.
key w KeyW control
key l KeyL -
scene
key w KeyW control
key h KeyH -
scene

# `C-w H` on the docked window moves it back to the end of the tiled list:
# no window is docked, so there is no strip, and the two windows are main
# and the stack. `C-w H` again docks it.
key w KeyW control
key H KeyH shift
scene
key w KeyW control
key H KeyH shift
scene

# `C-w m` makes the docked window main: main's old window is the stack,
# and there is no strip.
key w KeyW control
key m KeyM -
scene

# `C-w H` docks it again, and `C-w C-c` closes it: the strip goes, and
# view 0 has the tiled area, focused.
key w KeyW control
key H KeyH shift
key w KeyW control
key c KeyC control
scene

# `C-w H` on the last tile is refused, and the echo area says why.
key w KeyW control
key H KeyH shift
scene
